{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/axylo-matrix.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,re\np=Path('acceptance/matrix.json')\nrows=json.loads(p.read_text())\nby={r['id']:r for r in rows}\nbase='packages/axylo/test/acceptance/'\ndef add(id,typ,title,file,kind='unit',registration=None):\n ref={'kind':kind,'file':base+file+'.test.ts','title':title}\n if registration: ref['registration']=registration\n by[id].setdefault('evidence',{}).setdefault(typ,[]).append(ref)\ndef exact(template, **parts):\n for key,val in parts.items(): template=template.replace('\"'${'\"'+key+'}',val)\n return template\ndiag='F3 \"'${type}: ${test.code} ${test.name}'\"'\nfocus=\\\"A2 \"'${type}: at every datum the keyboard reaches, the focus indicators (the plot'\"'s outline and the ring around the datum) are painted at least 2 px wide and 3:1 against their painted backdrop, and the tooltip covers neither them nor the focused datum (reading: no part of either indicator is covered)\\\"\npalette='A5 \"'${type}: the eight painted colours (${scheme} scheme) are each at least 3:1 on their painted backdrop and at least 0.10 apart in OKLab under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia, analytic and as an 8-bit image'\"'\ngrouped=\\\"A5 bar: grouped bars of different series are separated by at least 1 px of background\"'${horizontal ? '\"' (horizontal bars)' : ''}: geometry, and painted pixels against a 1 px control\\\"\nslide=\\\"A7 \"'${type}: with the plot focused, a sliding window keeps focus on its datum: the value text is not rewritten while the datum stays (decision 0004), the numeric position follows it, eviction moves focus to the next datum once, and the next key reads the current count\"\nmessage_keys=\"A10 ${type}: every built-in string that a ${type} chart shows is replaced through messages: each applicable key'\"'s own sentinel reaches a reader surface, and no built-in English is left\\\"\nmessage_lang='A10 \"'${type}: on a lang=\"de\" page the built-in English is marked lang=\"en\" where the reader meets it: the description the figure references, the visible summary, the note, the controls, the plot'\"\\\\'s name and role; the author\\\\'s title is not'\naxe=\\\"A8 \"'${type.startsWith('\"'compact') ? 'compact' : type}: axe-core reports no violations on the whole landmarked page in every state (\"'${type}: ${states(type).map(s => s.name).join('\"', ')}, and with values left out), each state checked to hold before the scan\\\"\nfor row in rows:\n for field in ['evidence','weak']:\n  for kind, refs in row.get(field,{}).items():\n   updated=[]\n   for ref in refs:\n    title=ref.get('title','')\n    file=ref['file']\n    type=title.split()[1].rstrip(':') if re.match(r'\"'^[AF]'\"\\\\d+ [a-z]+:',title) else kind\n    if 'dx-diagnostics' in file:\n     if 'AX104 parses signed' in title or 'AX109 warns about seconds' in title: ref['registration']=diag\n     if 'AX141 reports a low-contrast resolved theme and draws with the same paint binding' in title:\n      title=title.replace('reports a low-contrast resolved theme and draws with the same paint binding','reports low contrast from the host’s resolved backdrop and preserves the paint binding')\n     if 'AX142 replaces a too-small' in title: continue\n    if 'keyboard focus indicator is at least' in title and 'a2-keyboard.browser' in file:\n     title,ref['registration']=exact(focus,type=type),focus\n    if 'a4-table.browser' in file:\n     title=title.replace('is identified and described in visible text','is identified, described in visible text and associated with the field')\n     if title.endswith('zoomed in, the table covers the current x range only'): title+=', row by row'\n    if 'a5-not-colour-alone.browser' in file:\n     if 'the eight rendered colours' in title:\n      title=exact(palette,type=type,scheme='light' if '(light scheme)' in title else 'dark')\n     title=title.replace(\\\"(the first series colour itself)\\\", \\\"(the first series' painted colour itself)\\\")\n     title=title.replace(\\\"along a vertical through the stack\\\", \\\"measured across the boundary\\\")\n     if 'stacked segments are separated' in title:\n      title='A5 bar: stacked segments are separated by at least 1 px of background in every stack: geometry, and painted pixels against a 1 px control'\n     if 'grouped bars of different series are separated' in title:\n      for whether in ['', ' (horizontal bars)']:\n       updated.append({**ref,'registration':grouped,'title':grouped.replace(\\\"\"'${horizontal ? '\"' (horizontal bars)' : ''}\\\",whether)})\n      continue\n     if 'adjacent slices are separated' in title:\n      title=\\\"A5 donut: each of the four seams of the ring, the closing one at 12 o'clock included, is at least 1 px of background against a 1 px control at the same angle\\\"\n     if 'in a grayscale screenshot' in title:\n      title=\\\"A5 line: in grayscale, each of three crossing traces' last-point marker has the shape class of its legend marker and differs from the other two by shape class (whether a reader can follow the crossing lines remains a human judgement)\\\"\n    if 'a6-a10.browser' in file:\n     if 'with the plot focused, ' in title:\n      if 'appended rows do not change' in title: continue\n      title=exact(slide,type=type)\n     if title.startswith('A10 ') and 'every built-in string is replaced' in title:\n      title=exact(message_keys,type=type)\n     if title.startswith('A10 ') and 'lang=\\\"de\\\"' in title:\n      title=exact(message_lang,type=type)\n     if title.startswith('A8 ') and 'in any state' in title:\n      for subject in ['compact','compact area','compact bar'] if type=='compact' else [type]:\n       states=['default']\n       if type\"'!='\"'compact': states+=['keyboard focus with tooltip','pointer tooltip','table open','streaming, paused']\n       if type in ['line','area','scatter']: states+=['zoomed']\n       if type in ['line','area','bar','scatter']: states+=['a series hidden']\n       states+=['loading','empty','error']\n       title=f\\\"A8 {type}: axe-core reports no violations on the whole landmarked page in every state ({subject}: {', '.join(states)}, and with values left out), each state checked to hold before the scan\\\"\n       updated.append({**ref,'registration':axe,'title':title})\n      continue\n    if file=='tests/dist/types.test.ts':\n     title=title.replace('read the declarations from the fixture node_modules, never from the workspace','read every declaration from inside the fixture, the packed ones from its node_modules')\n    if file=='tests/dist/csp.browser.test.ts':\n     title=title.replace('catch text inserted as HTML: the observer records the element and the policy reports the inline handler and style','catch text inserted as HTML: the observer records the element, and each report names its directive and page')\n    if file=='tests/dist/first-chart.browser.test.ts':\n     title=title.replace('renders under StrictMode (setup, cleanup, setup) with one chart left','renders under StrictMode with one chart left')\n     if 'the AX104 hint is printed' in title:\n      dev=title.startswith('development')\n      for loader in ['ESM', 'script tag']:\n       flavour = f'ESM, {\\\"development condition (axylo.dev.js)\\\" if dev else \\\"production condition (axylo.js)\\\"}' if loader=='ESM' else f'script tag, {\\\"development (axylo.iife.js)\\\" if dev else \\\"production (axylo.iife.min.js)\\\"}'\n       updated.append({**ref,'file':'tests/dist/flavours.browser.test.ts','title':f'hints print {\\\"once\\\" if dev else \\\"never\\\"}, are delivered either way, and warnings print once',\n        'registration':\\\"hints print \"'${flavour.development ? '\"'once' : 'never'}, are delivered either way, and warnings print once\\\",\n        'ancestors':[flavour]})\n      continue\n    if title: ref['title']=title\n    updated.append(ref)\n   row[field][kind]=updated\nfor id in ['L1','L3','C3']:\n for kind, refs in by[id]['evidence'].items():\n  by[id]['evidence'][kind]=[ref for ref in refs if ref['kind']=='browser']\nfor kind in ['line','area','bar','scatter','donut']:\n by['L1']['gaps'][kind]='Browser checks use fixed fixtures. Generated labels, late fonts and any historical text-zoom failures require a current browser run.'\n by['L8']['gaps'][kind]='The Node model varies width, container height and caption height. A browser must establish the one-line summary and controls in the resulting figure.'\n by['A3']['gaps'] = by['A3'].get('gaps',{})\n by['A3']['gaps'][kind]='Chrome can verify the focused accessibility-tree name and live-region text after each key. Current evidence checks DOM state and modeled readout text.'\n by['A3']['cannotVerify'][kind]='Record the screen-reader rehearsal on NVDA with Chrome and Firefox, VoiceOver with macOS Safari and iOS, and TalkBack with Chrome, including touch gesture reachability.'\nfor id,kind in [('I2','donut'),('A7','compact')]:\n by[id]['appliesTo'].append(kind)\n del by[id]['notApplicable'][kind]\nby['I2']['pending']={'donut':'Donut has a legend under F8 and the toggle rule does not exempt slices. Click, Enter, Space and the pressed state need a donut legend test.'}\nadd('A7','compact','A7 compact: appends update the static summary quietly in line, area and bar','reader-model')\nby['A7']['gaps']['compact']='A quiet append is verified in all three Node variants. Browser live-region and 24-chart checks are pending. The point-focus requirement applies where the chart has point navigation.'\nfor kind in ['line','area']:\n add('F2',kind,f'F2 {kind}: an isolated value between two gaps is drawn at its coordinates below 12 px spacing','f-missing-values')\nadd('F2','scatter',\\\"F2 scatter: appending unplottable values retains their table rows and missing zero only imputes missing values\\\",'f-missing-values')\nadd('F3','line','F3 line: AX140 reaches the reader and prints once without a title in production','production')\nadd('F3','scatter','F3 scatter: AX106 retains an all-string non-decimal column only in the table','dx-diagnostics',registration=diag)\nfor gaps in [1000,1001]:\n for kind in ['number','wall-clock']:\n  add('F3','line',f'F3 line: AX105 distinguishes {gaps} absent steps on a {kind} axis','dx-diagnostics',registration=diag)\nadd('F8','donut','F8 donut: zero and null slices count toward the eight-slice limit without gaining arcs','f-donut')\nby['F8']['gaps']['donut']='The zero/null limit fixture checks whether every input slice counts. The current implementation counts only slices with arcs.'\nby['F5']['gaps']={\n 'line':'Node proves simplification on both device-pixel ratios and several zooms, including a dropped sample accessible by keyboard and table. Browser evidence for the current tree is pending.',\n 'area':'Node checks per-column cumulative extrema on the stacked boundaries and gaps on the component stroke. Access to a discarded area sample through keyboard and table is unverified.',\n 'compact':'Node checks simplified line and cumulative area geometry at two device-pixel ratios. Dense compact rendering in a browser is unverified.'}\nby['T-dense-area']['gaps']['area']=by['F5']['gaps']['area']\nby['T-dense-line']['gaps']={'line':by['F5']['gaps']['line']}\nfor kind in ['line','area','bar','scatter','compact']:\n by['F7']['gaps'][kind]=('All compact variants check data/reference extent and exact 4% or 0.04 bounds. Compact has no drawn ticks or zoom.'\n  if kind=='compact' else 'Both automatic ends are compared with the first enclosing drawn ticks, including small declared percent and ratio maxima. Zoom is modeled in Node.')\nfor kind in ['area','bar','compact']:\n by['F10']['gaps'][kind]=('Node checks both sides and missing height for both compact variants. The incomplete summary has no current rendered accessibility-tree check.'\n  if kind=='compact' else 'Per-cell signs, zero and missing values exercise both sides and the axis bounds. The reader model currently yields only the algebraic total for the mixed-sign fixture.')\nby['F3']['gaps']['compact']='The diagnostic registry has partial compact coverage, including compact area and bar for AX110. Code-by-variant delivery, level, and reader outcome are incomplete.'\n# Keep historical browser assertions cited only under their current source titles.\np.write_text(json.dumps(rows,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 /tmp/axylo-matrix.py\nnode acceptance/check.mjs >/tmp/axylo-check-structure.log 2>&1\nhead -16 /tmp/axylo-check-structure.log\nrg -n 'Test Files|Tests |\"'^ FAIL'\"' /tmp/axylo-mutations.log | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
